  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Cutting",
      "html": "<figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1774624722097-da20076c8958?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1774624722097-da20076c8958?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1774624722097-da20076c8958?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"Scissors and thread spools on fabric\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Good tools make better garments.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@pixelesse?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Ksenia Pixelesse</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure><ul><li><strong>Dressmaking shears</strong> kept for fabric only.</li><li><strong>Small snips</strong> for threads.</li><li><strong>Rotary cutter and self-healing mat</strong> for quilting and straight cuts.</li><li><strong>Seam ripper</strong>, because everyone needs one.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Measuring and marking",
      "html": "<p>A tape measure, a clear ruler, tailor’s chalk or erasable pens, and a seam gauge cover most jobs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Thread",
      "html": "<p>Use a good-quality polyester all-purpose thread for most sewing, and match the thread to the needle size. Cheap thread sheds lint into the machine and breaks more often.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Pressing and workshop kit",
      "html": "<p>An iron, pressing cloth and ham make seams look professional. Workrooms also need cutting tables, steam irons and heat presses. <a href=\"http://www.pksm.co.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">PK Sewing Machines</a> supplies pressing and cutting equipment, tables, motors and workshop essentials alongside machines.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Buttons, zips and notions",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Zips</strong>: regular, invisible (concealed) and open-ended for jackets. Match the length or buy longer and shorten.</li><li><strong>Buttons</strong>: sew-through or shank; buy a spare.</li><li><strong>Interfacing</strong>: fusible or sew-in, in weights to match the fabric.</li><li><strong>Elastic, bias binding and tape</strong>: worth keeping in stock.</li></ul><div class=\"fig-pair\"><figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531376653594-e9bcf0f0c65b?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531376653594-e9bcf0f0c65b?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1531376653594-e9bcf0f0c65b?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"Red and blue zips\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Zips come in regular, invisible and open-ended types.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@tomas_nz?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Tomas Sobek</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1742462925156-78e5009a9bbc?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1742462925156-78e5009a9bbc?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1742462925156-78e5009a9bbc?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"Buttons arranged neatly by colour\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Always buy a spare button.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@kovalskihelga?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Olga Kovalski</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure></div>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Machine care tools",
      "html": "<p>A lint brush, sewing machine oil (for machines that need it), small screwdrivers and spare needles keep a machine running between services.</p>"
    }
  ],
